Add esp32p4 (RISC-V rv32imafc + Xesppie, hard-float ilp32f, die v3.1+) as a
firmware target to the @embedded (firmware) module, after the C3 port's pattern
(docs/design/p4-c6-split.md §3.1):

 - nix: unzip esp32p4/ from the esp32-arduino-libs zip (same raw-zip hash) and
   stage it at sdk/esp32p4.
 - platforms: esp32p4_board, the esp32p4 platform, is_esp32p4.
 - toolchains/cc/esp32p4: -march=rv32imafc_zicsr_zifencei_xesploop_xespv
   -mabi=ilp32f (every object in the image must be ilp32f).
 - MODULE.bazel: register it; the riscv32imafc-unknown-none-elf Rust triple.
 - rules/firmware.bzl: board esp32p4.
 - libs/board: core_esp32p4, esp32p4.cpp, esp32p4_bootloader_bin (the P4 ROM
   loads it from 0x2000: esptool_flash bootloader_offset).
 - libs/pins: LED_DATA_PIN=20 placeholder.
 - libs/vendor: preferences selects preferences_esp32p4 (NVS, for the P4 player);
   boot_app0 (the otadata image), for the P4 image's bundle of the C6 images.
 - nix/arduino_esp32.BUILD: the esp32p4 section, GENERATED from the libs'
   esp32p4/flags/* by tools/gen_embedded_p4_section.py. mbedTLS stays the
   prebuilt (the P4 player terminates no TLS). BOARD_HAS_PSRAM brings up PSRAM.

